How does one handle errors with MESH?<p>To handle errors in HTMX, I like to use config from [0] to swap responses into error dialogs and `hx-on-htmx-send-error` [1] and `hx-on-htmx-response-error` [2] to show the dialogs.  For some components, I also use an `on-htmx-error` attribute handler:<p><pre><code>    &#x2F;&#x2F; https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;events&#x2F;
    document.body.addEventListener(&#x27;htmx:error&#x27;, function (event: any) {
        const elt = event.detail.elt as HTMLElement
        const handlerString = elt.getAttribute(&#x27;on-htmx-error&#x27;)
        console.log(&#x27;htmx:error evt.detail.elt.id=&#x27; + elt.getAttribute(&#x27;id&#x27;) + &#x27; handler=&#x27; + handlerString)
        if (handlerString) {
            eval(handlerString)
        }
    });
</code></pre>
This gives very good UX on network and server errors.<p>[0]: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;quirks&#x2F;#by-default-4xx-5xx-responses-do-not-swap" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;quirks&#x2F;#by-default-4xx-5xx-responses-do-not...</a><p>[1]: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;events&#x2F;#htmx:sendError" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;events&#x2F;#htmx:sendError</a><p>[2]: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;events&#x2F;#htmx:responseError" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;htmx.org&#x2F;events&#x2F;#htmx:responseError</a>
